{"content":[{"c":["ZABDIEL"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. Father of Jashobeam, the commander of the first division of David’s army (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.27.2","r":"1Chr.27.2","rawR":"1Chr.27.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.27.2","value":"1Chr.27.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 27:2"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2. Priest and overseer of 128 “mighty men of valor” (",{"c":["rsv"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"},", ",{"href":"?bref=Neh.11.14","r":"Neh.11.14","rawR":"Neh.11.14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.11.14","value":"Neh.11.14"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 11:14"},"). The notation that he was a “son of Haggedolim” might indicate that he was a “son of the mighty men.”"],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["3. Arab who beheaded Alexander (Balas) Epiphanes and sent the head to Ptolemy (",{"href":"?bref=1Macc.11.17","r":"1Macc.11.17","rawR":"1Macc.11.17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Macc.11.17","value":"1Macc.11.17"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Macc 11:17"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Zabdiel","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"1 Chr 27:2","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.27.2","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.27.2","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.27.2"},{"anchorText":"Neh 11:14","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.11.14","rawQueryValue":"Neh.11.14","sourceRefExact":"Neh.11.14"},{"anchorText":"1 Macc 11:17","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Macc.11.17","rawQueryValue":"1Macc.11.17","sourceRefExact":"1Macc.11.17"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"54fac1ce61416d2073804f78788bd095e44178a29083257315bd0b6bb139ceb8","sourceItemName":"Zabdiel","sourceItemOrder":9,"sourceMember":"Articles/Z.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Zabdiel","product":"Tyndal